From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 03:53:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: ave: probe the T8132 (M4) encoder,
 probe only

The J604 (MacBook Pro 14", M4, T8132) runtime ADT describes its video
encoder as /arm-io/ave, compatible "ave2", pre-loaded, with

  __TEXT  0x148000 bytes at device address 0x10000000000
  __DATA  0x12c000 bytes at device address 0x10000148000

and the 25G83 boot stub's AppleAVE2FW_H16G (AppleAVE2FW-9003.78.0) has the
same segment sizes (TEXT CRC32 9308d2ab, DATA 56015462 in the IPSW image).
The T6041 (M4 Pro) runs H16S with a 0x14c000-byte TEXT, so the T8132 needs
its own variant.

What the driver needs beyond the sizes, the boot device ID and device
type the firmware handshake carries and the coprocessor register layout,
is not known for the T8132 yet. Add the variant as probe only: no
coprocessor registers and boot_qualified false. ave_fw_probe() then
checks the bootloader hand-off (two apple,asc-mem reservations, their
DART mappings, the loader CRCs in /chosen) and logs

  probe only: firmware TEXT <crc> DATA <crc> needs qualification

while ave_fw_check_boot() refuses every start, so the coprocessor is
never touched. Match apple,t8132-ave, which the binding already lists.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/media/platform/apple/ave/ave-drv.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/ave/ave-drv.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/ave/ave-drv.c
index c145e29538..cd7ac47bad 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/ave/ave-drv.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/ave/ave-drv.c
@@ -100,6 +100,22 @@ static const struct ave_variant ave_t6041 = {
 	.boot_qualified = true,
 };
 
+/*
+ * The M4 (T8132, J604 MacBook Pro) runs AppleAVE2FW_H16G 9003.78.0 from the
+ * 25G83 boot stub: __TEXT 0x148000 and __DATA 0x12c000 bytes, as the J604 ADT
+ * segment-ranges and the IPSW firmware image both give. Its boot device ID,
+ * device type and coprocessor registers are not known, so the variant is
+ * probe only: ave_fw_probe() records the CRCs of the preloaded segments and
+ * ave_fw_check_boot() refuses to start the coprocessor (no regs, not
+ * qualified). Nothing here touches the coprocessor.
+ */
+static const struct ave_variant ave_t8132 = {
+	.fw_text_size = 0x148000,
+	.fw_data_size = 0x12c000,
+	.lfs_ref_scale = 2,
+	.boot_qualified = false,
+};
+
 static const struct ave_variant ave_t8140 = {
 	.regs = &ave_coproc_v40,
 	.fw_text_size = 0x14c000,
@@ -391,6 +407,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id ave_of_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "apple,t6000-ave", .data = &ave_t6000 },
 	{ .compatible = "apple,t6041-ave", .data = &ave_t6041 },
 	{ .compatible = "apple,t8112-ave", .data = &ave_t8112 },
+	{ .compatible = "apple,t8132-ave", .data = &ave_t8132 },
 	{ .compatible = "apple,t8140-ave", .data = &ave_t8140 },
 	{}
 };
